    "statement_text": "I, Amit Verma, s/o Ramesh Verma, state that I work as delivery partner with Zomato. On 15th October 2024, I was delivering orders. At around 6:15 PM, I picked up an order from Haldiram's in Karol Bagh. The order was to be delivered in Old Rajinder Nagar, near Bada Bazaar within 20 minutes. I was going on my Pulsar motorcycle DL2SBP1234. The traffic signal at Shankar Road T-point was not working and there was a traffic policeman managing it. I was in a hurry to deliver the order because if I am late, my incentive gets cut. I admit that my speed was somewhat more but I thought I could cross the junction before the scooter turned. When I reached near the hospital T-point, I saw a white Activa scooter was turning from the other side. I tried to apply brakes but the distance was less and my bike collided with the scooter. I also fell down. When I got up, I saw the scooter rider was lying on the road and was injured. I got scared. The traffic policeman came and caught me. I was not trying to run away, I was just picking up my bike which had fallen. I admit my mistake. I should not have ridden at that speed. I had delivered 18 orders since morning and was tired. Please forgive me, I am a poor person. I have old parents in village. I will not repeat such mistake in future. I will bear all medical expenses of the injured person. Whatever happened was not intentional, it was a mistake because of hurry. I am ready to cooperate with the investigation.",
